{"id":"mahabharata-6-072","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":72,"title":"द्विसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 72 · Dhritarashtra marvels at his own army","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra praises the size, training and order of his army and wonders how it can be losing. He concludes that fate must have ordained it long ago.","kn":"ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ತನ್ನ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ಗಾತ್ರ, ತರಬೇತಿ, ಶಿಸ್ತನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳಿ ಅದು ಹೇಗೆ ಸೋಲುತ್ತಿದೆಯೆಂದು ಆಶ್ಚರ್ಯಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದೈವವೇ ಇದನ್ನು ಬಹುಕಾಲದ ಹಿಂದೆ ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸಿದೆ ಎಂದು ತೀರ್ಮಾನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र अपनी सेना के आकार, प्रशिक्षण और व्यवस्था की प्रशंसा करते हैं और आश्चर्य करते हैं कि वह कैसे हार रही है। वे निष्कर्ष निकालते हैं कि दैव ने यह बहुत पहले तय कर दिया था।","te":"ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు తన సైన్యం పరిమాణం, శిక్షణ, క్రమాన్ని పొగిడి అది ఎలా ఓడిపోతున్నదని ఆశ్చర్యపడతాడు. దైవమే దీన్ని ఎప్పుడో నిర్ణయించిందని తేల్చుకుంటాడు.","ta":"த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் தன் படையின் அளவு, பயிற்சி, ஒழுங்கைப் புகழ்ந்து அது எப்படித் தோற்கிறது என்று வியக்கிறான். இது விதியால் முன்பே விதிக்கப்பட்டது என்று முடிவு செய்கிறான்.","ml":"തന്റെ സേനയുടെ വലുപ്പത്തെയും പരിശീലനത്തെയും ക്രമത്തെയും ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു; അത് എങ്ങനെ തോറ്റുപോകുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം അത്ഭുതപ്പെടുന്നു. വളരെ മുൻപേ വിധി അങ്ങനെ നിശ്ചയിച്ചിരുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം നിഗമനത്തിലെത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.72; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवं बहुगुणं सैन्यमेवं बहुविधं परम् ।\nव्यूढमेवं यथाशास्त्रममोघं चैव संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"An army so rich in virtues, so varied and excellent, drawn up so according to the texts, and never failing, Sanjaya,"}},{"n":2,"text":"पुष्टमस्माकमत्यन्तमभिकामं च नः सदा ।\nप्रह्वमव्यसनोपेतं पुरस्ताद्दृष्टविक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"always well fed, always eager for us, humble, free of vice, whose valor was seen before,"}},{"n":3,"text":"नातिवृद्धमबालं च न कृशं न च पीवरम् ।\nलघुवृत्तायतप्रायं सारगात्रमनामयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"neither too old nor a child, neither thin nor stout, light in step and tall, strong-bodied and healthy,"}},{"n":4,"text":"आत्तसंनाहशस्त्रं च बहुशस्त्रपरिग्रहम् ।\nअसियुद्धे नियुद्धे च गदायुद्धे च कोविदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with armor and weapons in hand, carrying many weapons, skilled in sword-fighting, wrestling and mace-fighting,"}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रासर्ष्टितोमरेष्वाजौ परिघेष्वायसेषु च ।\nभिण्डिपालेषु शक्तीषु मुसलेषु च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"in the use of lances, spears and javelins in battle, in iron clubs, in bhindipalas, spears and pestles everywhere,"}},{"n":6,"text":"कम्पनेषु च चापेषु कणपेषु च सर्वशः ।\nक्षेपणीषु च चित्रासु मुष्टियुद्धेषु कोविदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"in vibrating bows, in kanapas, in slings and various missiles, and in boxing,"}},{"n":7,"text":"अपरोक्षं च विद्यासु व्यायामेषु कृतश्रमम् ।\nशस्त्रग्रहणविद्यासु सर्वासु परिनिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"well versed in the sciences, practiced in exercises, perfectly skilled in all the arts of handling weapons,"}},{"n":8,"text":"आरोहे पर्यवस्कन्दे सरणे सान्तरप्लुते ।\nसम्यक्प्रहरणे याने व्यपयाने च कोविदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"expert in mounting, dismounting, advancing, leaping aside, striking well, marching and retreating,"}},{"n":9,"text":"नागाश्वरथयानेषु बहुशः सुपरीक्षितम् ।\nपरीक्ष्य च यथान्यायं वेतनेनोपपादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"well tested many times in elephant, horse and chariot driving, tested rightly and supplied with wages,"}},{"n":10,"text":"न गोष्ठ्या नोपचारेण न च बन्धुनिमित्ततः ।\nन सौहृदबलैश्चापि नाकुलीनपरिग्रहैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"not chosen by flattery or favor, nor by kinship, nor by friendship's strength, nor taken from low families,"}},{"n":11,"text":"समृद्धजनमार्यं च तुष्टसत्कृतबान्धवम् ।\nकृतोपकारभूयिष्ठं यशस्वि च मनस्वि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"of prosperous people and nobles, whose kin are satisfied and honored, who have often been given favors, renowned and high-minded,"}},{"n":12,"text":"सजयैश्च नरैर्मुख्यैर्बहुशो मुख्यकर्मभिः ।\nलोकपालोपमैस्तात पालितं लोकविश्रुतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"protected, my dear, by chief men of many great exploits, victorious, like guardians of the world, famed in the world,"}},{"n":13,"text":"बहुभिः क्षत्रियैर्गुप्तं पृथिव्यां लोकसंमतैः ।\nअस्मानभिगतैः कामात्सबलैः सपदानुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"guarded by many kshatriyas, esteemed in the world, who have come to us out of desire, with their forces and followers,"}},{"n":14,"text":"महोदधिमिवापूर्णमापगाभिः समन्ततः ।\nअपक्षैः पक्षसंकाशै रथैर्नागैश्च संवृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"like the great ocean full on every side with rivers, covered with chariots and elephants like winged ones without wings,"}},{"n":15,"text":"नानायोधजलं भीमं वाहनोर्मितरङ्गिणम् ।\nक्षेपण्यसिगदाशक्तिशरप्राससमाकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"its water the many warriors, terrible, with the waves and ripples of its mounts, filled with slings, swords, maces, spears, arrows and lances,"}},{"n":16,"text":"ध्वजभूषणसंबाधं रत्नपट्टेन संचितम् ।\nवाहनैः परिसर्पद्भिर्वायुवेगविकम्पितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"crowded with the ornaments of banners, heaped with jeweled cloths, shaken by the wind-speed of moving vehicles,"}},{"n":17,"text":"अपारमिव गर्जन्तं सागरप्रतिमं महत् ।\nद्रोणभीष्माभिसंगुप्तं गुप्तं च कृतवर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"roaring as if without shore, like the great sea, guarded by Drona and Bhishma, and guarded by Kritavarma,"}},{"n":18,"text":"कृपदुःशासनाभ्यां च जयद्रथमुखैस्तथा ।\nभगदत्तविकर्णाभ्यां द्रौणिसौबलबाह्लिकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"by Kripa and Duhshasana, by Jayadratha and others, by Bhagadatta and Vikarna, by Drona's son, Shakuni's son and Bahlika,"}},{"n":19,"text":"गुप्तं प्रवीरैर्लोकस्य सारवद्भिर्महात्मभिः ।\nयदहन्यत संग्रामे दिष्टमेतत्पुरातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"guarded by heroes who are the strength of the world, great-souled men: that this was struck in battle is ancient fate."}},{"n":20,"text":"नैतादृशं समुद्योगं दृष्टवन्तोऽथ मानुषाः ।\nऋषयो वा महाभागाः पुराणा भुवि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Humans have not seen such an effort, nor have the great sages of old on earth, Sanjaya."}},{"n":21,"text":"ईदृशो हि बलौघस्तु युक्तः शस्त्रास्त्रसंपदा ।\nवध्यते यत्र संग्रामे किमन्यद्भागधेयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When such a flood of troops, equipped with the wealth of weapons and missiles, is struck down in battle, what else can it be but destiny?"}},{"n":22,"text":"विपरीतमिदं सर्वं प्रतिभाति स्म संजय ।\nयत्रेदृशं बलं घोरं नातरद्युधि पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this seems upside down to me, Sanjaya, that such a terrible army did not defeat the Pandavas in battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"अथ वा पाण्डवार्थाय देवास्तत्र समागताः ।\nयुध्यन्ते मामकं सैन्यं यदवध्यन्त संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or else the gods have come there for the Pandavas' sake and fight my army, so that it is killed, Sanjaya."}},{"n":24,"text":"उक्तो हि विदुरेणेह हितं पथ्यं च संजय ।\nन च गृह्णाति तन्मन्दः पुत्रो दुर्योधनो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vidura told me here what was good and wholesome, Sanjaya, but my foolish son Duryodhana does not accept it."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्य मन्ये मतिः पूर्वं सर्वज्ञस्य महात्मनः ।\nआसीद्यथागतं तात येन दृष्टमिदं पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think that his wise and great-souled foresight, my dear, was so, he who saw all this beforehand."}},{"n":26,"text":"अथ वा भाव्यमेवं हि संजयैतेन सर्वथा ।\nपुरा धात्रा यथा सृष्टं तत्तथा न तदन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or else, Sanjaya, it must in every way be so; as the Creator made it long ago, it is so and cannot be otherwise."}}]}]}